WEBVTT

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:20.330
It's so cold!

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:27.460
Restroom...

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:32.460
Yunocchi, are you up yet?

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:33.800
Miya-chan?

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.220
I am!

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:37.940
Morning, Yunocchi!

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:39.600
It's freezing today!

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:41.180
Hey, morning.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:43.390
Would you like some hot tea?

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:44.350
Yay!

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:47.270
Oh!

00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:48.520
An igloo.

00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:50.600
Huh?

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:09.250
youki ni kuchibue fuite

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:09.250
Whistling a cheerful tune

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:11.580
madobe no kotori to sesshon

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:11.580
I join the birds chirping by the window

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:14.500
suima ga yatte kite

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:14.500
When fatigue strikes

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:17.130
atama ga danshingu

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:17.130
My imagination runs wild

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:19.590
nan demo kan demo waraeru nichijou

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:19.590
Everything in life makes me smile

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:22.430
okimari na kishoutenketsu

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:22.430
Nothing really new takes place

00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:25.060
demo demo tama ni wa piritto supaisu

00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:25.060
But sometimes it's exciting to spice things up

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:27.680
aozora peintingu

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:27.680
Let's paint it on the blue sky

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:28.730
doko ikou

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:28.730
Where should we go?

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:30.310
koko ni iyou

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:30.310
Let's stay here

00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:31.310
sore wa nani

00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:31.310
What's that?

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:32.900
are yaritai

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:32.900
I wanna try that!

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:35.480
ima ni tokubetsu na shirushi

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:35.480
Let's make this moment count

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:40.860
tokeibari no mawashikata watashi shidai kamo

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:40.860
How fast my clock moves is all up to me

00:01:42.110 --> 00:01:44.530
shiki oriori iro toridori

00:01:42.110 --> 00:01:44.530
With a rich palette of colors from the four seasons

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:46.990
nonbiri na everyday

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:46.990
Our laid-back everyday lives can be

00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:49.620
pasuteru bibiddo metoro

00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:49.620
Any blend of pastel, vivid, and metro colors

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:52.460
jibun dake no karaaringu

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:52.460
Anyone can create their own coloring

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:55.040
sono tokidoki mune doki doki

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:55.040
So when your heart races in excitement

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:58.760
hachamecha na taiyou ni oegaki

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:58.760
Just draw a sun at the top

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:02.890
tobidasu aatishizumu

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:02.890
And let your inner artist take you from there

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:06.220
gyutto shite ii kana

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:06.220
Can I hold your hand tight?

00:02:10.970 --> 00:02:13.600
suki suki suki wo sukecchi

00:02:10.970 --> 00:02:13.600
I've been sketching everything I love

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:16.140
nijiiro ni somete iku yo

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:16.140
And painting them in rainbow colors

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:20.900
sore ja ittekimasu

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:20.900
All right, I'm off to have some more fun!

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:26.120
December 22nd

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:26.120
So You Were the Big Sister

00:02:30.370 --> 00:02:33.330
This is the first time I've been to her house!

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:34.750
Me too, actually!

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:36.870
We've been here once before.

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:37.570
Right?

00:02:37.570 --> 00:02:39.880
Yeah, on New Year's Day.

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:42.880
Welcome, everybody!

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:45.630
Thanks for helping me out today!

00:02:45.630 --> 00:02:47.600
Hello, Sensei!

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.470
Now, if you don't mind...

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:56.310
If any of you have cell phones with cameras, I'll be holding onto them.

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:57.190
What?

00:02:57.190 --> 00:02:58.060
Huh?

00:02:58.060 --> 00:02:59.060
Also...

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:02.630
Could you sign here, please?

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:08.490
All right!

00:03:08.490 --> 00:03:10.950
You look ready to roll, Yuno-san!

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:14.530
I'm counting on you guys!

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:19.000
You see,

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:27.550
I've amassed too many art books in my room,
so I want to donate some of them to Yamabuki.

00:03:27.550 --> 00:03:29.650
But there are quite a few books,

00:03:29.650 --> 00:03:32.770
so it'd be great if a few of you could help me carry them.

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:36.750
Did a tornado come through here?

00:03:38.270 --> 00:03:40.890
I'll put all the Western art stuff here,

00:03:40.890 --> 00:03:42.900
and the other books here.

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:45.030
There's a lot of magazines over here.

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:47.790
Could you sort them by genres for now?

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:48.910
Got it.

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:51.510
I didn't sign up for this.

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:53.910
Oh, I just remembered.

00:03:53.910 --> 00:03:58.830
I'm looking for a few things, so I'd appreciate it if you kept an eye out for those as well.

00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:00.670
Huh? What are they?

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:05.550
Your first sketches from when you had just enrolled in Yamabuki got lost under the piles of books.

00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:06.770
From when we...

00:04:06.770 --> 00:04:07.800
...had just enrolled?

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:11.300
Thanks so much!

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:18.560
Is this...

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:21.390
an elementary school yearbook?

00:04:21.390 --> 00:04:22.170
What?

00:04:22.170 --> 00:04:24.290
Can we look inside, Sensei?

00:04:24.290 --> 00:04:25.320
Go ahead!

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:30.990
This is Yoshinoya-sensei, isn't it?

00:04:30.990 --> 00:04:32.580
Oh, it is!

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:33.950
She's so adorable!

00:04:33.950 --> 00:04:34.950
This is awesome!

00:04:34.950 --> 00:04:36.830
Let's see what else is in here!

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:48.420
All right, let's put some elbow grease into this and get it over with!

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:49.430
Yeah!

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:52.150
These giant art books are so heavy!

00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:53.310
Thanks!

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:55.650
Do we have the entire series now?

00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:58.170
Can I put all the art magazines here?

00:04:58.170 --> 00:04:58.810
Sure.

00:04:58.810 --> 00:04:59.690
Okay!

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:03.440
Are the exhibition catalogs still over there?

00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:05.450
I don't see any.

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:06.790
Okay!

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:09.820
Miya-chan!

00:05:08.980 --> 00:05:09.820
Sorry!

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:14.630
Why don't you take a little break?

00:05:14.630 --> 00:05:16.410
I'll prepare some tea!

00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:18.910
Oh, thank you.

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:21.920
I'm exhausted.

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:35.470
Good morning!

00:05:35.470 --> 00:05:36.630
Please wake up!

00:05:36.630 --> 00:05:37.560
Let's wake up!

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:42.850
You'll be late for school if you don't get up now!

00:05:42.850 --> 00:05:44.810
Pull yourself together and get up!

00:05:44.810 --> 00:05:46.810
I realize that you're sleepy...

00:05:46.810 --> 00:05:48.850
It's hard to get through the morning, isn't it?

00:05:48.850 --> 00:05:49.710
But...

00:05:49.710 --> 00:05:51.030
Oh, five minutes!

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:53.320
You can sleep in for just five more minutes.

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:54.530
Sensei...

00:05:54.530 --> 00:05:58.810
If it's just five minutes, you can still make it as long as you run!

00:05:58.810 --> 00:06:02.030
If worse comes to worst, you can skip your delicious breakfast and...

00:06:02.030 --> 00:06:04.430
No, that'd be terrible!

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:06.830
Let's just stick to running!

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:09.840
In that case, you should probably wake up soon.

00:06:11.920 --> 00:06:13.390
She's not very...

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:14.680
...disciplined.

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:19.430
Okay, it's ready!

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:23.830
This place is a lot tidier thanks to you all!

00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:25.550
I really appreciate it!

00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:26.810
Oh, you're welcome.

00:06:26.810 --> 00:06:28.490
Oh, right.

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:31.090
If you'd like, in return for helping me out,

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:35.170
feel free to take a book home.

00:06:35.170 --> 00:06:35.770
What?

00:06:35.770 --> 00:06:37.200
Thanks!

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:40.150
Are you sure about this?

00:06:40.150 --> 00:06:41.410
It's all right!

00:06:41.410 --> 00:06:43.460
I was going to donate them anyway.

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:46.450
Besides, even if I don't read them anymore,

00:06:46.450 --> 00:06:51.340
I've already read them so many times that they're part of my soul now!

00:06:52.590 --> 00:06:56.240
I'm giving you parts of my soul!

00:06:56.240 --> 00:06:57.590
On second thought, we'll pass.

00:07:02.420 --> 00:07:03.100
Oh!

00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:05.370
I think that's everything.

00:07:05.370 --> 00:07:07.230
Now we just need to take them to school.

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:09.190
Thank you, everyone!

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:16.230
Huh? That sounded like a person.

00:07:16.920 --> 00:07:19.990
He said he'd be late today.

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:21.990
I'm back!

00:07:21.990 --> 00:07:24.000
Oh, you have students over?

00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:27.670
Sensei, what's the meaning of this?

00:07:27.670 --> 00:07:28.710
Wow!

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:30.070
Y-You even have a child?!

00:07:30.070 --> 00:07:32.010
I never thought you'd...

00:07:35.010 --> 00:07:36.570
Sorry, Sis.

00:07:36.570 --> 00:07:37.590
Am I interrupting something?

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:38.760
"Sis"?

00:07:38.760 --> 00:07:41.470
I wanted to bring him to see Mom and Dad.

00:07:41.470 --> 00:07:42.850
Are they out?

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:44.290
Yeah, they are.

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:46.020
It's been a while, Kento-kun!

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:48.020
It's been a while, Auntie!

00:07:48.020 --> 00:07:50.020
It's not "Auntie," remember?

00:07:50.020 --> 00:07:51.650
It's "Princess"!

00:07:51.650 --> 00:07:52.730
Remember?

00:07:52.730 --> 00:07:54.610
At least make it "Sissy"!

00:07:55.150 --> 00:07:56.930
Up you go!

00:07:57.840 --> 00:08:02.160
I'm three years younger than her, but I got married first.

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:03.850
I almost had a heart attack!

00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:07.160
You don't look much like Yoshinoya-sensei.

00:08:08.180 --> 00:08:09.290
I get that a lot.

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:12.610
It was especially bad when I started middle school.

00:08:12.610 --> 00:08:16.720
Every single teacher I met had this expression of relief on their face, and they said,

00:08:16.840 --> 00:08:19.490
"When I heard Yoshinoya's little brother was coming,

00:08:19.490 --> 00:08:21.570
I was so worried about what kind of person he'd turn out to be."

00:08:21.570 --> 00:08:22.650
And I mean <i>every</i> teacher!

00:08:22.650 --> 00:08:24.560
It got annoying quick.

00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:28.470
I bet she's one heck of a homeroom teacher.

00:08:28.470 --> 00:08:30.950
Just to make sure, is she really a teacher?

00:08:30.950 --> 00:08:33.320
You still don't believe me?!

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:40.090
We should take these to school before it gets too dark.

00:08:40.090 --> 00:08:42.030
You mean the books?

00:08:42.030 --> 00:08:44.080
I drove here, so you wanna take them in my car?

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:45.080
Huh?

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:48.750
That's everything!

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:50.330
Okay, great!

00:08:54.210 --> 00:08:56.070
Wow, we managed to fit everything!

00:08:56.070 --> 00:08:57.250
It's so spacious!

00:08:57.250 --> 00:08:59.030
All right, everyone, hop in!

00:08:59.030 --> 00:08:59.970
Okay!

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:03.230
Make sure you drive safely, okay?

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:05.490
Of course you should always be careful,

00:09:05.490 --> 00:09:08.730
but my students are coming along, so be five times more careful!

00:09:09.100 --> 00:09:10.730
Sensei...

00:09:16.180 --> 00:09:18.530
After all that worrying...

00:09:18.530 --> 00:09:20.780
She fell asleep.

00:09:20.780 --> 00:09:22.630
She's sound asleep.

00:09:26.020 --> 00:09:29.330
I got into a traffic accident when I was little.

00:09:29.330 --> 00:09:31.790
I was lucky and only suffered minor injuries,

00:09:31.790 --> 00:09:34.830
but Sis cried so much over it.

00:09:34.830 --> 00:09:37.610
She cried so hard that it took me forever to get her to calm down.

00:09:38.420 --> 00:09:41.680
So you should all be careful too!

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:44.670
Or she'll cry like a baby again.

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:47.510
Got it.

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:55.390
Today was so fun!

00:09:55.390 --> 00:09:58.250
Yeah. We had some surprises too.

00:09:58.820 --> 00:10:00.820
Oh, welcome back!

00:10:00.820 --> 00:10:03.390
Everyone else is here, so why don't you stop by for some tea?

00:10:03.390 --> 00:10:04.450
Okay!

00:10:06.450 --> 00:10:09.510
Yuno-san, Miyako-san, welcome back!

00:10:09.510 --> 00:10:10.950
Glad to be back!

00:10:10.950 --> 00:10:12.790
I'll make some tea now.

00:10:12.790 --> 00:10:14.770
Thanks so much!

00:10:15.780 --> 00:10:17.710
What are those books? Did you buy them?

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:23.210
Nah, we were at Sensei's all day helping her clean up.

00:10:23.210 --> 00:10:25.220
Yoshinoya-sensei gave them to us!

00:10:25.220 --> 00:10:26.780
Right?

00:10:26.780 --> 00:10:27.470
Huh?

00:10:27.470 --> 00:10:29.250
Something fell out.

00:10:29.250 --> 00:10:29.850
Oh!

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:31.390
What a nice photo!

00:10:31.390 --> 00:10:32.730
It must've been stuck between the pages.

00:10:32.730 --> 00:10:33.600
You're right!

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:36.100
We should give it back to her.

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:39.790
What is this photo?!

00:10:39.790 --> 00:10:41.230
Who is this man?!

00:10:41.230 --> 00:10:43.030
Oh, don't jump to conclusions just yet!

00:10:43.030 --> 00:10:45.790
Um... You see, this person is...

00:10:45.790 --> 00:10:47.050
What is it?

00:10:48.300 --> 00:10:50.370
That's Sensei's little brother!

00:10:50.370 --> 00:10:51.750
Little brother?

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:53.500
Oh, little brother?

00:10:53.500 --> 00:10:54.950
Her little brother, huh?

00:10:54.950 --> 00:10:57.460
I figured as much.

00:10:57.460 --> 00:10:58.590
Oh, so that was all.

00:10:58.590 --> 00:11:02.050
They don't look like each other.

00:11:02.050 --> 00:11:04.550
People say that a lot, apparently.

00:11:04.550 --> 00:11:06.430
He brought his son too.

00:11:06.430 --> 00:11:07.430
His son?!

00:11:07.430 --> 00:11:08.470
He has a kid?

00:11:08.470 --> 00:11:09.410
He does!

00:11:09.410 --> 00:11:11.270
He's around elementary school age.

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:12.850
His name's Kento-kun!

00:11:12.850 --> 00:11:14.730
He's a cute little guy!

00:11:14.730 --> 00:11:18.020
And he called Yoshinoya-sensei "Auntie"!

00:11:18.020 --> 00:11:19.070
"Auntie"?

00:11:19.070 --> 00:11:22.090
Oh yeah, she <i>is</i> his aunt, technically.

00:11:22.090 --> 00:11:24.930
Her little brother must've gotten married early.

00:11:24.930 --> 00:11:28.280
I wonder if Sensei is feeling pressured to get married soon.

00:11:28.280 --> 00:11:31.380
I think it might be the opposite.

00:11:31.380 --> 00:11:34.990
She might be relieved to see her
little brother have a good family.

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:38.670
That's way off in the future for me, so I have no clue.

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:41.340
Well, a lot of things happen in life.

00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:44.310
Getting married isn't all there is to it.

00:11:44.310 --> 00:11:47.460
Sae, that's not a good follow-up.

00:11:47.460 --> 00:11:48.510
Really?

00:11:49.300 --> 00:11:50.250
Far.

00:11:50.250 --> 00:11:51.960
Too far ahead.

00:11:51.960 --> 00:11:56.060
I can't think about things too
far in the future right now!

00:11:56.060 --> 00:11:57.910
Is something wrong?

00:11:57.910 --> 00:12:00.250
Miya-chan, are you feeling hungry?

00:12:00.250 --> 00:12:01.450
You got it!

00:12:01.450 --> 00:12:03.690
We got a lot of work done today, after all.

00:12:03.690 --> 00:12:06.810
I've been starving forever!

00:12:06.810 --> 00:12:09.450
Then I guess we should start making dinner.

00:12:09.450 --> 00:12:11.170
Okay!

00:12:24.370 --> 00:12:26.010
Oh, Natsume!

00:12:26.010 --> 00:12:27.520
What are you doing?

00:12:27.520 --> 00:12:28.780
S-Sae!

00:12:28.780 --> 00:12:30.120
Wh-What?

00:12:30.120 --> 00:12:31.360
I'm not doing anything.

00:12:31.360 --> 00:12:32.800
I'm going home.

00:12:32.800 --> 00:12:34.240
You are too, right?

00:12:34.240 --> 00:12:35.040
Yeah.

00:12:35.630 --> 00:12:36.780
See you, then.

00:12:36.780 --> 00:12:38.780
Oh, you wanna stop by my place?

00:12:38.780 --> 00:12:40.050
What?

00:12:40.050 --> 00:12:40.900
Huh?

00:12:40.900 --> 00:12:42.120
Hidamari Apartments, I mean.

00:12:42.120 --> 00:12:43.620
You said you wanted to visit.

00:12:43.620 --> 00:12:45.660
You only saw the garden last time.

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:48.700
Out of nowhere? And right now?

00:12:48.700 --> 00:12:51.160
How can you invite someone so spontaneously?

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:51.720
Huh?

00:12:51.720 --> 00:12:53.920
Well, sorry.

00:12:53.920 --> 00:12:57.120
All right. I still have to ask the others about this,

00:12:57.120 --> 00:12:59.300
but would you like to join us for our Christmas Eve party?

00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:03.300
What?!

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:05.440
Ch-Christmas?!

00:13:05.440 --> 00:13:06.460
Are you sure?

00:13:06.460 --> 00:13:07.920
Yeah, I think so.

00:13:07.920 --> 00:13:10.310
Oh, do you have plans already?

00:13:10.310 --> 00:13:12.310
N-Not at all!

00:13:12.310 --> 00:13:14.600
Then I'll get in touch with you later.

00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:17.300
Something wrong?

00:13:19.280 --> 00:13:20.240
See you!

00:13:22.090 --> 00:13:23.320
Am I dreaming?

00:13:24.150 --> 00:13:25.570
Ouch!

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:30.580
December 21st-24th,
A Song I Faintly Remember

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:34.940
Oh, there's the permission from the party host.

00:13:34.940 --> 00:13:37.090
It'll be seven people this year, then!

00:13:37.090 --> 00:13:40.340
"We'll be preparing the food this year,

00:13:40.340 --> 00:13:46.140
so please bring a gift under 1000 yen and an empty stomach to the party."

00:13:46.140 --> 00:13:47.920
It's going to be so much fun!

00:13:47.920 --> 00:13:51.980
"I recommend that Hiro-san lose a kilo of weight until then."

00:13:52.980 --> 00:13:55.500
I bet that was Miya-chan chiming in!

00:13:55.500 --> 00:13:57.110
See ya.

00:13:58.360 --> 00:14:00.360
Jingle bells, jingle bells!

00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:06.490
Christmas is here!

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:07.980
Hey!

00:14:07.980 --> 00:14:09.240
Yunocchi!

00:14:10.490 --> 00:14:12.600
Miya-chan, were you listening?

00:14:12.600 --> 00:14:14.750
The first-years behind me were too.

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:19.940
I'll put the fried chicken here.

00:14:19.940 --> 00:14:22.880
I made Christmas okonomiyaki!

00:14:24.670 --> 00:14:26.130
That's so cute!

00:14:29.390 --> 00:14:31.600
Alrighty! We're ready to go!

00:14:31.600 --> 00:14:32.640
Amazing!

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:34.600
Thanks for cooking, guys.

00:14:35.490 --> 00:14:37.460
Now we just need Natsume-san to get here.

00:14:37.460 --> 00:14:41.900
Yeah, she texted saying she was at the station just now, so she should be here soon.

00:14:42.590 --> 00:14:43.840
So...

00:14:43.840 --> 00:14:45.650
Room 201, right?

00:14:48.110 --> 00:14:49.280
It's open!

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:51.280
U-Um...

00:14:51.280 --> 00:14:52.300
Welcome!

00:14:52.300 --> 00:14:54.160
Welcome, Natsume-san!

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:55.410
Good evening!

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:57.420
G-Good evening!

00:14:57.870 --> 00:14:59.790
Go ahead and come on in!

00:15:00.430 --> 00:15:02.170
Okay, thanks.

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:08.020
Natsume-san, long time no see!

00:15:08.020 --> 00:15:09.550
Long time no see!

00:15:09.550 --> 00:15:12.560
Yeah, thanks for inviting me today.

00:15:13.560 --> 00:15:16.060
Then let's get right down to it!

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:17.560
Okay!

00:15:18.010 --> 00:15:19.440
Cheers!

00:15:19.440 --> 00:15:21.690
Merry Christmas!

00:15:21.690 --> 00:15:23.190
Merry Christmas.

00:15:23.820 --> 00:15:26.190
Grab all the food you want!

00:15:26.190 --> 00:15:27.700
Alrighty!

00:15:27.700 --> 00:15:30.280
Now this is the five-star treatment!

00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:31.420
Same here.

00:15:31.420 --> 00:15:34.460
It's Christmas. You can't <i>always</i> be the one stuck with the cooking

00:15:34.460 --> 00:15:36.930
Thanks, everyone!

00:15:36.930 --> 00:15:38.460
I'll help myself, then.

00:15:40.920 --> 00:15:42.940
This fried chicken is delish!

00:15:42.940 --> 00:15:45.000
I made that!

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:45.920
What?

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:48.090
You can make fried food all by yourself?

00:15:48.090 --> 00:15:52.140
Uh, fried chicken's about all I can make, though.

00:15:52.140 --> 00:15:54.720
You trained me well last time, after all!

00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:55.470
Yeah!

00:15:59.090 --> 00:16:00.600
It's delicious!

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:02.730
It's juicy and really well-done!

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:04.320
Glad you like it!

00:16:05.570 --> 00:16:08.070
Have my okonomiyaki too!

00:16:08.070 --> 00:16:10.320
It's authentic Kansai style!

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:11.720
What?

00:16:11.720 --> 00:16:15.080
My sandwiches are also authentic—

00:16:15.290 --> 00:16:18.200
What country do sandwiches come from again?

00:16:18.200 --> 00:16:21.040
Not Japan, that's for sure.

00:16:24.590 --> 00:16:27.320
Let's cut the cake up!

00:16:29.870 --> 00:16:31.050
What's wrong?

00:16:31.050 --> 00:16:32.880
I-It's gonna fall!

00:16:35.060 --> 00:16:36.560
I'm sorry!

00:16:36.560 --> 00:16:37.930
I got this!

00:16:37.930 --> 00:16:38.980
Miya-chan, here!

00:16:38.980 --> 00:16:40.480
Thanks, Yunocchi.

00:16:40.480 --> 00:16:42.260
Natsume-san, here goes!

00:16:42.260 --> 00:16:43.310
Okay!

00:16:43.310 --> 00:16:44.810
One, two...

00:16:44.810 --> 00:16:46.320
There!

00:16:53.770 --> 00:16:54.570
Huh?

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:57.800
I don't usually get along with most people.

00:16:57.800 --> 00:17:00.330
Everyone ends up getting along in this place.

00:17:02.850 --> 00:17:04.460
It's so good!

00:17:04.460 --> 00:17:06.780
The strawberry is so sweet!

00:17:06.780 --> 00:17:08.090
I'm glad with how it turned out!

00:17:08.920 --> 00:17:11.040
So this was homemade too.

00:17:12.650 --> 00:17:13.680
It's good!

00:17:17.060 --> 00:17:19.180
And now what you've all been waiting for!

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:20.860
Time to exchange gifts!

00:17:20.860 --> 00:17:22.040
Bang!

00:17:22.690 --> 00:17:24.440
Wait, bananas?

00:17:24.440 --> 00:17:27.780
As you eat the banana, you'll see a name written on the stick,

00:17:27.780 --> 00:17:29.940
and you get that person's gift!

00:17:29.940 --> 00:17:31.280
Oh, you're right.

00:17:31.280 --> 00:17:33.120
There's something written on it.

00:17:33.120 --> 00:17:34.450
This is elaborate.

00:17:35.350 --> 00:17:37.700
Mine says, "You win!"

00:17:37.700 --> 00:17:39.260
Mine does too.

00:17:39.260 --> 00:17:40.480
What's this mean?

00:17:40.480 --> 00:17:42.580
Congratulations!

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:45.200
That means you get another!

00:17:45.200 --> 00:17:47.460
What? One more?

00:17:47.910 --> 00:17:50.800
Bananas fill you up quickly, don't they?

00:17:50.800 --> 00:17:52.050
Let's see...

00:17:52.050 --> 00:17:54.460
Mine is... Miyako-chan?

00:17:55.930 --> 00:17:58.260
Here you go! This is my gift!

00:17:58.260 --> 00:17:58.810
What?

00:18:03.180 --> 00:18:04.360
Oh!

00:18:04.360 --> 00:18:06.270
It's an Alongcat hug pillow.

00:18:06.270 --> 00:18:06.900
That's huge!

00:18:06.900 --> 00:18:07.810
What's that?

00:18:07.810 --> 00:18:08.900
You don't know?

00:18:08.900 --> 00:18:11.520
Alongcat! Sleep alongside a long cat!

00:18:11.520 --> 00:18:13.700
The size is what makes it great!

00:18:13.700 --> 00:18:15.240
It's really bulky.

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:17.700
Are you sure you can take that on the train when you go home?

00:18:17.700 --> 00:18:21.060
You can take it out of the bag and set it next to you.

00:18:21.060 --> 00:18:23.240
Wouldn't that look super suspicious?

00:18:23.710 --> 00:18:26.130
And Natsume-san gave me...

00:18:26.130 --> 00:18:28.460
a Christmas tree cultivation kit!

00:18:28.460 --> 00:18:29.620
This is wonderful!

00:18:29.620 --> 00:18:30.380
You like it?

00:18:30.380 --> 00:18:31.220
Yeah!

00:18:31.220 --> 00:18:32.630
I'm really happy!

00:18:32.630 --> 00:18:34.510
I'm glad to hear that.

00:18:34.510 --> 00:18:36.400
And Nazuna gave me...

00:18:36.400 --> 00:18:37.440
a handkerchief!

00:18:37.440 --> 00:18:39.010
And a wristwatch?

00:18:39.010 --> 00:18:40.010
Yeah.

00:18:40.010 --> 00:18:45.020
I won the wristwatch in the raffle with tickets I got when I bought the handkerchief.

00:18:45.020 --> 00:18:48.100
Whoa, then you should keep it!

00:18:48.100 --> 00:18:49.840
It's probably some luxury watch!

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:51.650
I can't accept it!

00:18:51.650 --> 00:18:52.650
I just can't!

00:18:54.370 --> 00:18:56.140
Let's just share it, then.

00:18:57.160 --> 00:18:59.180
Sae-san gave me...

00:18:59.180 --> 00:19:00.900
a premium ballpoint pen!

00:19:00.900 --> 00:19:03.120
It was 1000 yen, so it's not really premium.

00:19:03.530 --> 00:19:05.820
I got a pendant from Yuno.

00:19:05.820 --> 00:19:09.170
I got a nail polish set from Hiro-san!

00:19:09.170 --> 00:19:11.570
And Nori-chan gave me...

00:19:11.570 --> 00:19:12.420
Huh?

00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:14.620
A rain check?

00:19:14.620 --> 00:19:19.180
I'm sorry. They told me that they were out of stock after I placed the order.

00:19:19.180 --> 00:19:22.430
Later you'll get a cheesecake that's ranked number one in deliver—

00:19:28.690 --> 00:19:29.690
Oh!

00:19:29.690 --> 00:19:31.780
I should start heading back now.

00:19:31.780 --> 00:19:33.480
What, already?

00:19:33.480 --> 00:19:34.810
Yeah.

00:19:34.810 --> 00:19:36.690
Then I'll see you to the station.

00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:38.900
It's all right!

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:40.140
I remember how to get there.

00:19:40.140 --> 00:19:42.100
You have this big gift to carry.

00:19:42.100 --> 00:19:43.240
I'm going, then.

00:19:45.080 --> 00:19:47.080
Please hold on a minute!

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:49.750
You don't visit often, so let's take a group photo!

00:19:52.750 --> 00:19:54.460
I had a lot of fun!

00:19:54.460 --> 00:19:55.600
Me too!

00:19:55.600 --> 00:19:57.560
We hope you come over again.

00:19:57.560 --> 00:19:58.800
We'll be waiting.

00:19:58.800 --> 00:20:01.510
Have fun with the Alongcat!

00:20:01.510 --> 00:20:02.570
I will!

00:20:02.570 --> 00:20:04.220
Thank you, everyone!

00:20:04.640 --> 00:20:06.390
Good-bye!

00:20:04.640 --> 00:20:06.390
See you!

00:20:12.470 --> 00:20:14.360
How did you like Hidamari Apartments?

00:20:14.360 --> 00:20:17.070
It was cheerful and a lot of fun.

00:20:17.070 --> 00:20:19.080
I imagined what it'd be like to live there,

00:20:19.080 --> 00:20:20.660
but now I've experienced the real thing.

00:20:21.310 --> 00:20:25.160
It was just like the feeling I got from "Us At Daybreak."

00:20:25.160 --> 00:20:25.910
What?

00:20:25.910 --> 00:20:29.260
You mean the short story I wrote last year?

00:20:29.260 --> 00:20:30.420
<i>Oh no!</i>

00:20:35.750 --> 00:20:38.420
Do you read my stories?

00:20:38.420 --> 00:20:39.920
Y-Yeah.

00:20:40.930 --> 00:20:42.680
More or less.

00:20:44.590 --> 00:20:47.480
Though I was just reading them casually at first...

00:20:47.480 --> 00:20:51.560
You know, your novels have really romantic settings,

00:20:51.560 --> 00:20:55.720
but they all feature realistic, imperfect characters.

00:20:55.720 --> 00:20:57.190
That aspect is...

00:20:57.190 --> 00:20:58.320
Huh?

00:20:58.320 --> 00:21:00.570
She reads and understands my stories.

00:21:01.820 --> 00:21:04.380
M-Merry Christmas!

00:21:04.910 --> 00:21:07.160
M-Merry...

00:21:11.750 --> 00:21:13.250
I'm back.

00:21:14.170 --> 00:21:16.720
Sae-san, welcome back.

00:21:16.720 --> 00:21:20.320
You didn't get into a fight the moment you two were left alone, did you?

00:21:20.320 --> 00:21:21.160
Nah.

00:21:21.850 --> 00:21:23.800
Then, something good must've happened to her.

00:21:25.170 --> 00:21:28.420
I guess Alongcat will come in handy right away!

00:21:28.420 --> 00:21:29.890
Huh? Alongcat?

00:21:29.890 --> 00:21:30.890
How come?

00:21:34.250 --> 00:21:37.150
She found out!

00:21:37.150 --> 00:21:39.650
How am I supposed to face her now?

00:21:46.700 --> 00:21:47.700
I'm full!

00:21:48.050 --> 00:21:49.370
I'm so happy!

00:21:49.770 --> 00:21:53.920
When I was little, I really believed in Santa.

00:21:53.920 --> 00:21:57.630
I wonder if he'd come if I went to bed right after my bath.

00:21:59.380 --> 00:22:03.960
Jingle bells, jingle bells, ru-ru ru-ru ru...

00:22:05.050 --> 00:22:08.140
Christmas is here!

00:22:08.140 --> 00:22:09.220
Hey!

00:22:15.560 --> 00:22:20.900
suikomaresou na gurai harebare shita asa no hi

00:22:15.560 --> 00:22:20.900
The bright morning sun lifts my soul up to the sky

00:22:20.900 --> 00:22:24.150
mezamashi no beru naru

00:22:20.900 --> 00:22:24.150
When my alarm clock rings

00:22:26.110 --> 00:22:29.120
furisosogu hikari ukete

00:22:26.110 --> 00:22:29.120
Soaking in the sunshine

00:22:29.120 --> 00:22:31.740
kokoro no kyoukaisen wo

00:22:29.120 --> 00:22:31.740
I once again cross

00:22:31.740 --> 00:22:35.540
saa kyou mo tobikoeyou

00:22:31.740 --> 00:22:35.540
My mental boundaries

00:22:35.540 --> 00:22:40.090
hikoukigumo sora ni mau

00:22:35.540 --> 00:22:40.090
With vapor trails behind me

00:22:41.170 --> 00:22:45.720
egaiteru tabi no tochuu

00:22:41.170 --> 00:22:45.720
I find myself in the middle of a journey

00:22:46.470 --> 00:22:53.220
omoide wa tsuzuiteru

00:22:46.470 --> 00:22:53.220
Carrying on memories in the sky

00:22:53.220 --> 00:22:55.770
machiawase wa mada saki e

00:22:53.220 --> 00:22:55.770
I'm still a long way from you

00:22:55.770 --> 00:22:58.730
mada mada mienai mukou

00:22:55.770 --> 00:22:58.730
We'll meet far beyond the horizon

00:22:58.730 --> 00:22:59.810
ruuru wa nai

00:22:58.730 --> 00:22:59.810
No rules here

00:22:59.810 --> 00:23:04.030
jiyuu ni hanatsu kyanbasu

00:22:59.810 --> 00:23:04.030
I can let it all out on this canvas

00:23:04.030 --> 00:23:06.700
kokoro to karada no baransu

00:23:04.030 --> 00:23:06.700
The balance between mind and body

00:23:06.700 --> 00:23:09.370
tenbin no ue de yureru

00:23:06.700 --> 00:23:09.370
Keeps shifting between the two

00:23:09.370 --> 00:23:14.620
atarashii aozora de donna yume wo miru

00:23:09.370 --> 00:23:14.620
I can dream of anything in a clean blue sky

00:23:14.620 --> 00:23:18.670
ima no kono basho wa

00:23:14.620 --> 00:23:18.670
From where I am at present

00:23:18.670 --> 00:23:24.590
mirai e tsunagaru kara

00:23:18.670 --> 00:23:24.590
I should be able to find a way to the future

00:23:24.590 --> 00:23:30.050
sagashiteru yumegumo

00:23:24.590 --> 00:23:30.050
And so I continue searching for my dream cloud

00:23:30.050 --> 00:23:35.850
doko ni aru no kana

00:23:30.050 --> 00:23:35.850
I wonder where it could be

00:23:40.230 --> 00:24:10.260
Next Episode

00:23:41.080 --> 00:23:43.570
Tell us about your year!

00:23:43.570 --> 00:23:44.210
Okay!

00:23:44.210 --> 00:23:45.890
I ate a lot and played a lot!

00:23:45.890 --> 00:23:47.030
I studied some too!

00:23:47.030 --> 00:23:49.010
I learned how to make fried chicken!

00:23:49.010 --> 00:23:50.510
I made a lot of wonderful memories!

00:23:50.510 --> 00:23:52.390
I did my personal best!

00:23:52.390 --> 00:23:53.500
Wonderful!

00:23:53.500 --> 00:23:56.330
Keep challenging yourself for the future!

00:23:56.330 --> 00:23:57.570
Yeah!

00:23:57.570 --> 00:24:00.350
I hope next year is another great year!

00:24:00.350 --> 00:24:05.630
Next time: "December 31st-January 1st, A Year Going Out, A Year Coming In."

00:24:05.630 --> 00:24:09.050
We'll be waiting at Hidamari Apartments, so come visit us!
